<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-AWB Australia wheat indicator prices - March 24.</title>
<headline>RTRS-AWB Australia wheat indicator prices - March 24.</headline>
<dateline>MELBOURNE 1997-03-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australian Wheat Board international card prices for wheat exports for March 24.</p>
<p>In U.S. dollars per tonne, FOB eastern states.</p>
<p>		ASW	  AH     PH 13 PCT  PH 14 PCT</p>
<p>    Mar    203.50    208.00    209.00     222.00</p>
<p>    Apr    201.50    206.00    207.00     222.00</p>
<p>    May    201.50    206.00    207.00     222.00</p>
<p>    Jun    197.00    201.50    202.50     220.00</p>
<p>    Jul    195.50    200.00    201.50     218.50</p>
<p>    Aug    194.50    199.00    200.00     217.50</p>
<p>Note: ASW = Australian Standard White; AH = Australian Hard; PH = Australian Prime Hard; percentages = protein content.</p>
<p>Australian Wheat Board indicator prices for multi-grade contracts for 1997/98 crop wheat decreased A$2.00 per tonne.</p>
<p>	  Indicator Prices in A$ per tonne:</p>
<p>		  ASW 10 pct protein</p>
<p>National FOB	174.00</p>
<p>Indicator prices on a delivered port basis:</p>
<p> Queensland			   South Australia</p>
<p>    Mackay	  149.50	    Port Adelaide	 151.00</p>
<p>    Gladstone     149.75	    Port Giles	    151.75</p>
<p>    Brisbane	147.50	    Wallaroo		149.50</p>
<p> New South Wales			Port Pirie	    146.50</p>
<p>    Newcastle     149.50	    Port Lincoln	  152.75</p>
<p>    Port Kembla   150.00	    Thevenard	     147.75</p>
<p>Victoria			     Western Australia</p>
<p>    Geelong	 149.00	     Esperance	    154.25</p>
<p>    Portland	150.00	     Albany		 155.25</p>
<p>					     Fremantle	    157.25</p>
<p>					     Geraldton	    155.25</p>
<p>NOTE: The indicator price represents the current state of the international wheat market. It is a cash contract fob price quoted on a delivered port basis, offered today by the AWB for wheat delivered during the 1997/98 harvest. The offer is valid until 4.30 p.m. Australian Eastern Summer Time (0530 GMT).</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
